7	 * panel's events (notes, the controls), moves each voice's pitch on
8	 * (glide, the pitch envelope, KNOB1) and sets its operators' phase steps,
9	 * then hands core 1 its voices, renders its own, waits for core 1 and
10	 * mixes. Voice allocation and stealing, mono with legato and glide, and
11	 * M4's test tone on PLAY are here too. Core 1 runs fm_core1_main.
12	 * Since M6a MIDI's messages arrive here too, after the panel's events
13	 * (docs/DESIGN-NOTES.md, M6a): notes from both, held apart so neither
14	 * ends the other's, the sustain pedal, pitch bend, vibrato, the
15	 * controller map, program changes and the channel modes.
16	 * Since M6b the panel's notes, knobs and program changes go to MIDI out,
17	 * MIDI thru passes on what MIDI in receives, and local control off keeps
18	 * the panel from playing the engine (docs/DESIGN-NOTES.md, M6b).
19	 */
